      "message": "feat(drilling): ream cycle (G85) as a drill operation parameter\n\nReam is a new cycle choice and CL cycle kind: feed in, feed back out at\nthe same feed, no dwell (RS-274/NGC G85, NIST IR 6556). Canned-cycle\nposts write G85 and refuse an unknown cycle word by name instead of\nposting it as another cycle; Heidenhain, TinyG and Carvera post the\nexpanded feed-out chain; posts without drilling refuse it. The ream\nrides the bore door (tool must fit, stepped hole refused, pre-drilled)\nand is never chosen by Auto. Command, project file, MCP edit_operation\nand the drill page's Cycle combo carry it; programs that do not choose\nit post byte-identical.\n\nRefs #1445\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
